class.description:
[method ResourceSaver.save] writes an [ImageTexture] or an [Image] to .png, .jpg, .jpeg, .webp, .exr and .dds files. Its flags cannot carry encoder settings, so they are set in an [ImageSaveOptions] that is attached to the saved resource with [method attach_to]. Without attached options, the defaults of [method Image.save_jpg], [method Image.save_webp] and [method Image.save_exr] are used. PNG and DDS have no options.
The options are stored as metadata on the resource (key [code]image_save_options[/code]). They are not shared between resources and not global, so saving from several threads at once is safe. If the resource itself is saved as [code].tres[/code] or [code].res[/code], the attached options are saved with it.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var image = Image.create_empty(64, 64, false, Image.FORMAT_RGBA8)
image.fill(Color.CORNFLOWER_BLUE)
var texture = ImageTexture.create_from_image(image)

var options = ImageSaveOptions.new()
options.webp_lossy = true
options.webp_quality = 0.8
options.attach_to(texture)
ResourceSaver.save(texture, "user://textures/blue.webp")

# Back to the defaults.
ImageSaveOptions.detach_from(texture)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var image = Image.CreateEmpty(64, 64, false, Image.Format.Rgba8);
image.Fill(Colors.CornflowerBlue);
var texture = ImageTexture.CreateFromImage(image);

var options = new ImageSaveOptions();
options.WebpLossy = true;
options.WebpQuality = 0.8f;
options.AttachTo(texture);
ResourceSaver.Save(texture, "user://textures/blue.webp");

// Back to the defaults.
ImageSaveOptions.DetachFrom(texture);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] Encoders that are disabled in a custom build (for example [code]module_webp_enabled=no[/code]) are not available; saving to their extension then fails with [constant ERR_FILE_UNRECOGNIZED].
